  "viewer_summary": "21 analytic and numerical unit tests pass. Twenty-four direction/wavelength comparisons used 500,000 Monte Carlo paths each. Lunar spot differences were below 0.7%; Earth differences reached 7%, with sampling errors recorded separately. These are selected tests, not whole-sky error bounds. Whole-sphere energy accounting leaves up to 4.6% residual in the lunar cases. A 64-to-128-shell ray check changes sampled radiances by up to 0.65%. Deeper-night playback is exploratory. Browser controls and offline embedded-data loading were tested through the software fallback; the exact GPU shaders separately compile and link in OpenGL ES. No empirical Earth-sky benchmark or physical lunar-atmosphere validation has been completed."
